# Bug 5, Bug 6, Bug 7: Compile-time parser bugs in normalize() and task()

Customers is a collection.
Each customer has a handle (text) and a score (number).
No two customers share the same handle.
If a customer already exists, reject it.

Bookings is a collection.
# Bug 5: Field "customer" on Bookings globally shadows the "Customers" collection!
Each booking has a booking_id (number) and a customer (text).
No two bookings share the same booking_id.
If a booking already exists, reject it.

# Fails because "customer" is now normalized as ('FIELD', 'customer'), not ('COLL', 'customer')!
add-customer: add a customer.

Orders is a collection.
Each order has an id (number) and a price (number).
No two orders share the same id.
If an order already exists, reject it.

# Bug 6: "order by" matches 2-word SORTBY in lexicon.py:90, hiding collection "order"!
find-order: find an order by id.

# Bug 7: Taught phrase with "is" instead of CMP fails without "whose"
"cheap" means price is 10.
cheap-orders: show the orders cheap.
